claim.claim-text:
a stowable support surface comprising a translucent display (105), the stowable support surface configured to be moveable between a first position and a second position;
at least one projector (125) configured to project an image (130) on the translucent display (105);
at least one sensor (305) configured to indicate a current position of the stowable support surface; and
a projector controller (135) in communication with the at least one projector (125) and the at least one sensor (305), wherein the projector controller (135) is programmed to:

instruct the at least one projector to project at least one image (130) on the translucent display (105) when the stowable support surface is in the first position;
receive a signal from the at least one sensor (305) indicating that the stowable support surface is in between the first position and the second position; and
instruct the at least one projector (125) to halt projection of images (130).

receiving a first signal from a first sensor (305);
determining a first projection sequence to activate in response to the first signal from the first sensor (305);
transmitting instructions to a first projector (125) to project the first projection sequence onto a projection face (115) of a first translucent display (105) of a stowable support surface in a stowed position, such that the first projection sequence is displayed on a display face (110) of the first translucent display (105), wherein the projection face (115) is an opposite side of the first translucent display (105) from the display face (110) of the first translucent display (105);
receiving a second signal from a second sensor (305) indicating a change in position of the first translucent display (105);
determining to halt projection of the first projection sequence in response to the second signal; and
transmitting instructions to the first projector (125) to halt projection of the first projection sequence.
